DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTSTAMP:20261108T165507Z
UID:bb5f79eb8f81bdfadb4237343e66@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:There are over 450 species of birds found in Connecticut\, and
  only a handful are not native to the state. The effects these birds have 
 on the environment and on us vary\, and some have become among the most co
 mmon\, and well-loved\, birds in the state. In this webinar\, Conservation
  & Education Coordinator Joe Attwater will discuss which species have been
  introduced to Connecticut and how they got here\, as well as the effects 
 introduced species can have on our native birds.\n\nSource: https://ctvisi
 t.com/events/introduced-bird-webinar
LOCATION:via Zoom\, 100 Lyme Street\, Old Lyme CT\, 06371
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/introduced-bird-webinar
END:VEVENT
